OW_SCOPE","final_urls":["https://api.github.com/repos/paperclipai/paperclip/commits?path=README.md\u0026per_page=1","https://api.github.com/repos/paperclipai/paperclip/readme?ref=8f0c1d45484e10d60bd99149a3b8a6d4c1798b77"],"primary_body_sha256":"sha256:e534958eedeeeb641c980e2a2b5e23143743f83bdf5a2866b2697a46944263aa","primary_commit":"8f0c1d45484e10d60bd99149a3b8a6d4c1798b77","primary_evidence_ref":{"content_hash":null,"entity_type":"Evidence","id":"ca145ff827850b98cf4b3c25c0044fea","revision":1},"primary_excerpt":"manage AI agents for work","primary_locator":"README.md#intro","primary_snapshot_ref":{"content_hash":"sha256:e534958eedeeeb641c980e2a2b5e23143743f83bdf5a2866b2697a46944263aa","entity_type":"Artifact","id":"36aa06b71806e8863cf40b4ed6cd76bc","revision":1},"primary_url":"https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/blob/8f0c1d45484e10d60bd99149a3b8a6d4c1798b77/README.md","request_urls":["https://api.github.com/repos/paperclipai/paperclip/commits?path=README.md\u0026per_page=1","https://api.github.com/repos/paperclipai/paperclip/readme?ref=8f0c1d45484e10d60bd99149a3b8a6d4c1798b77"],"retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T20:11:44.3649734Z","unverified_claims":["Today's two strongest growth positions belong to memory and agent management. That combination points toward the systems needed to keep agents useful across tasks.","+2,420 stars in 1 day; 41,989 total. Learning-oriented memory leads the ranking, putting accumulated experience at the center of today's momentum.","+2,251 stars in 1 day; 93,960 total. Agent management and memory together gained 4,671 stars—the strongest infrastructure pairing in this snapshot.","+725 stars in 1 day; #20 → #8; 2,277 total. Centralizing model access across agents in a menu-bar interface makes tool-and-model combinations easier to manage.","+381 stars in 1 day; #31 → #14. Extracting, updating and pruning skills from real sessions brings skill upkeep into the working loop.","+326 stars in 1 day; #49 → #18. Local AST parsing and explained graph edges offer a structured way to organize code and supporting context.","+281 stars in 1 day; #32 → #22. Packaging design judgment as a skill makes quality requirements part of the agent workflow.","Stars show attention, not proven effectiveness. But the project mix is clear: agent value is expanding into maintainable experience, knowledge and runtime control."],"x_evidence_ref":{"content_hash":null,"entity_type":"Evidence","id":"6f08780b942791e20a89d2b0f2909a02","revision":1}},"db_path":"execution\\receipts\\W07\\run-3c1540e6c5d44deeaed6fbe97f0d0f2b\\live-X.sqlite"}
